 CORS allows only the configured frontend origin, including preflight requests with
 `Authorization`, `Content-Type`, and `X-Helpdesk-Account` headers. It does not enable cookies.
 
+## Invitations and people management
+
+All paths below are relative to `/api/v1` and require `X-Helpdesk-Account`. Except for
+preview and acceptance, they also require a verified, non-suspended user's bearer token.
+Only **admins** (not just the owner) may manage invitations or users. Admins and agents
+can work on all tickets in their business. Existing `member` users retain staff access,
+but new invitations may only use `admin` or `agent`.
+
+### Invitations
+
+| Method and path | Success response |
+| --- | --- |
+| `POST /invitations` | `201 {"invitation":{...}}`; admin-only, sends the invitation email |
+| `GET /invitations` | `200 {"invitations":[...],...pagination}`; admin-only |
+| `GET /invitations/:id` | `200 {"invitation":{...}}`; admin-only |
+| `POST /invitations/:id/resend` | `200 {"invitation":{...}}`; admin-only, sends a fresh link |
+| `DELETE /invitations/:id` | `204`; admin-only, revokes rather than deletes the invitation |
+| `POST /invitation_previews` | `200 {"invitation_preview":{...}}`; public, requires a valid token |
+| `POST /invitation_acceptances` | `201 {"user":{...},"account":{...}}`; public, consumes the token |
+
+Invite staff:
+
+```json
+{"invitation":{"email":"sam@example.test","role":"agent"}}
+```
+
+Invitation representations contain `id`, `account_id`, `email`, `role`, `status`,
+`expires_at`, `accepted_at`, `revoked_at`, `created_at`, and `updated_at`. Tokens and their
+digests are never returned. Status is `pending`, `accepted`, `revoked`, or `expired`.
+Filter lists using `?status=pending` (or another valid status).
+
+The email links to the configured frontend's
+`/accept-invitation?account=acme&token=TOKEN`. Links expire after **7 days**. Resending a
+pending or expired invitation rotates its token, immediately invalidating the old link,
+and starts a new 7-day lifetime. Accepted and revoked invitations cannot be resent;
+accepted invitations cannot be revoked. Repeated revocation is idempotent.
+
+Email reservations are case-insensitive and account-scoped. A registered user's email
+cannot be invited, and an unexpired pending invitation blocks both another invitation
+and customer registration for its email. Expired or revoked invitations release their
+reservation. Resending an expired invitation fails if its email has since been claimed.
+Account row locks serialize reservation and acceptance with registration and cancellation;
+a database unique index also prevents competing pending invitations.
+
+The frontend reads `account` from the link to set `X-Helpdesk-Account`, then previews it:
+
+```json
+{"invitation_preview":{"token":"TOKEN"}}
+```
+
+The response's `invitation_preview` contains `email`, `role`, `name` (business name),
+`subdomain`, and `expires_at`. Previewing does not consume the token. Invalid, expired,
+revoked, accepted, wrong-account, or wrong-purpose tokens return `422` without revealing
+invitation details. Cancelled accounts cannot preview or accept invitations.
+
+Accept with a name and a password of at least 8 characters:
+
+```json
+{"invitation_acceptance":{"token":"TOKEN","name":"Sam","password":"my-team-password"}}
+```
+
+Acceptance atomically creates a non-owner user with the invited email and role, marks
+that user verified, and consumes the invitation. No verification email is sent. The user
+can immediately sign in through `/sessions`; acceptance does not itself create a session.
+Invalid names or passwords leave the invitation usable.
+
+### Users and assignment choices
+
+| Method and path | Success response |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /users` | `200 {"users":[...],...pagination}`; admin-only |
+| `GET /users/:id` | `200 {"user":{...}}`; admin-only |
+| `PATCH /users/:id` | `200 {"user":{...}}`; admin-only, accepts `name` and/or `suspended` |
+| `GET /staff` | `200 {"staff":[...],...pagination}`; staff-only, verified and non-suspended staff |
+
+All user representations include the boolean `suspended`. Users can be filtered by
+`?role=agent`, `?suspended=true`, or both. Suspension query values must be `true` or
+`false`; JSON updates require real booleans:
+
+```json
+{"user":{"suspended":true}}
+```
+
+Suspension immediately revokes every session for that user and clears all of their ticket
+assignments. Login and recovery cannot bypass suspension. Unsuspending does not restore
+old sessions or assignments. The last verified, non-suspended admin cannot be suspended,
+even by themselves or by concurrent requests. Only the owner retains account cancellation
+and reactivation privileges. User updates cannot change email, role, account, ownership,
+or verification state.
+
+Invitation, user, and staff lists sort by **ID ascending**, using the same pagination
+metadata described below. Filters apply before counting and pagination; invalid filters
+return `400`. All lookups are scoped to the current account.
